   "title": "Problème — Circuit RLC série et résonance",
   "difficulty": 3,
   "validated": false,
   "params": {
    "R": {
     "unit": "",
     "values": [
      10,
      20,
      50
     ]
    },
    "L": {
     "unit": "",
     "values": [
      0.1,
      0.2,
      0.5
     ]
    },
    "C": {
     "unit": "F",
     "values": [
      1e-05,
      2.2e-05,
      4.7e-05
     ]
    },
    "f": {
     "unit": "",
     "values": [
      50,
      60,
      100
     ]
    }
   },
   "vars": {
    "w": "2*pi*f",
    "X": "L*2*pi*f - 1/(C*2*pi*f)",
    "Z": "R + j*(L*2*pi*f - 1/(C*2*pi*f))"
   },
   "constraints": [],
   "statement": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Un circuit comprend en série une résistance $R =$ [[R]] Ω, une bobine $L =$ [[L]] H et un condensateur $C =$ [[C]]. Il est alimenté par une tension sinusoïdale de valeur efficace 230 V et de fréquence $f =$ [[f]] Hz."
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "On note $\\underline{Z} = R + j\\left(L\\omega - \\dfrac{1}{C\\omega}\\right)$ son impédance complexe."
    }
   ],
   "questions": [
    {
     "id": "q1",
     "kind": "numeric",
     "prompt": "Pulsation ω (rad/s) ?",
     "answer": "w",
     "unit": "rad/s",
     "tolerance": 0.01,
     "sig": 3
    },
    {
     "id": "q2",
     "kind": "complex",
     "prompt": "Impédance complexe $\\underline{Z}$ (forme algébrique) ?",
     "answer": "Z",
     "tolerance": 0.02,
     "sig": 3,
     "polar": false
    },
    {
     "id": "q3",
     "kind": "numeric",
     "prompt": "Module de $\\underline{Z}$ (Ω) ?",
     "answer": "abs(Z)",
     "unit": "Ω",
     "tolerance": 0.01,
     "sig": 3
    },
    {
     "id": "q4",
     "kind": "numeric",
     "prompt": "Argument de $\\underline{Z}$ en degrés ?",
     "answer": "deg(arg(Z))",
     "unit": "°",
     "tolerance": 0.02,
     "sig": 3
    },
    {
     "id": "q5",
     "kind": "numeric",
     "prompt": "Valeur efficace du courant (A) ?",
     "answer": "230/abs(Z)",
     "unit": "A",
     "tolerance": 0.01,
     "sig": 3
    },
    {
     "id": "q6",
     "kind": "numeric",
     "prompt": "Fréquence de résonance $f_0 = \\dfrac{1}{2\\pi\\sqrt{LC}}$ (Hz) ?",
     "answer": "1/(2*pi*sqrt(L*C))",
     "unit": "Hz",
     "tolerance": 0.01,
     "sig": 3
    }
   ],
   "hint": "Calcule d'abord Lω et 1/(Cω).",
   "method": "1. ω = 2πf.\n2. Partie imaginaire X = Lω − 1/(Cω).\n3. Module √(R² + X²), argument arctan(X/R).\n4. I = U/|Z|.\n5. À la résonance, X = 0.",
   "solution": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "$\\omega \\approx$ [[=w:4|rad/s]] ; $X \\approx$ [[=X:3]] Ω, d'où $\\underline Z \\approx$ [[=Z:3]]."
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "$|\\underline Z| \\approx$ [[=abs(Z):3|Ω]], argument ≈ [[=deg(arg(Z)):3]]° ; $I \\approx$ [[=230/abs(Z):3|A]]."
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Résonance quand $LC\\omega^2 = 1$ : $f_0 \\approx$ [[=1/(2*pi*sqrt(L*C)):3|Hz]], où $|\\underline Z| = R$ est minimal."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "PB-M-02",
